        {
          "body": "Clear the consumed batch before invoking callback-capable saving, preserving new edits queued by synchronous callback reentry. Preserve empty text as valid work; do not replace the null check with a truthiness check or clear pending work after the callback. src/services.js: \"const flush = () => { const saved = value; retire(); if (saved !== null) consume(saved); };\"",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R03"
        },
        {
          "body": "Separate persistent document work from subscription cleanup. View retirement must not discard accepted edits or destroy reusable per-document tasks. docs/host-api.md: \"Document buffers are owned by a separate BufferBank service, while Badge owns only a live subscription.\" Survival does not alone mandate immediate flushing on departure; establish any such deadline independently.",
          "category": "preservation",
          "id": "R04"
        },
        {
          "body": "Preserve navigation authority around callback-capable saving. Capture the departing view, release current ownership before retirement callbacks, and clean up the captured subscription without clearing a newer view afterward. Retain the request check before installing an opening. src/coordinator.js: \"const old=getView();setView(null);\" and \"const mine=++request;retire();if(true&&mine!==request)return;\" docs/host-api.md: \"A store listener may call navigation synchronously.\" If departure-time saving is added, ensure subsequent outer mutations cannot overwrite nested navigation; place saving after final retirement mutations or recheck authority before continuing.",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R05"
        },
        {
          "body": "Preserve public interfaces, document display, live status filtering, and document identity, text, and status payload semantics. TASK: \"Preserve the editor's other behavior and public interfaces.\" docs/host-api.md: \"All source identities/text and status payloads retain original semantics.\" src/coordinator.js: \"if(event.id===id)env.renderStatus(event);\" Verify coordinator cleanup through the supplied React integration as well: src/Workspace.jsx contains \"useEffect(()=>api.dispose,[api]);\".",
