          "id": "R06"
        },
        {
          "body": "Keep transient search preview outside the repair, including its 40 ms delay, discard on hide, and subsequent reuse. TASK: \"The adjacent search preview is outside this maintenance change.\" src/services.js: \"const task = trailing(timers, 40, query => publish({query}));\" and \"return {query: text => task.push(text), hide: () => task.cancel()};\" Do not transfer persistent document ownership policy to preview or change its behavior through shared-utility edits.",
          "category": "exclusion",
          "id": "R07"
        },
        {
          "body": "Use controlled time to check no immediate write, latest text only after 120 ms of quiet, deadline restart, subsequent bursts, empty text, originating-document binding, and independent document buffers. Exercise switch, close, dispose, same-document reopening, subscription cleanup, save-triggered open/close, and callback-enqueued edits. Verify cleanup through both coordinator calls and React effect cleanup. Check preview delay, hide cancellation, and reuse. Require accepted document work to survive retirement; assert persistence before departure returns only with independent normative support. These checks derive from TASK's \"Subsequent bursts\nmust continue to save.\" and \"Preserve the editor's other behavior and public interfaces.\", together with the ownership, callback, and utility evidence above; evaluation observations remain examples.",
          "category": "verification",
          "id": "R08"
        }
